The ROS 2 interface definitions in firmware/msg/ (.msg, .srv, .action files) follow the
definitions of the ROS 2 packages they are named after (builtin_interfaces, std_msgs,
geometry_msgs, sensor_msgs, nav_msgs, tf2_msgs, rcl_interfaces, lifecycle_msgs,
action_msgs, unique_identifier_msgs, std_srvs, rosgraph_msgs, nav2_msgs), which are
distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Some unbounded arrays are given fixed
capacities on the chip (firmware/msg/capacities.txt); the CDR encoding is unchanged.

